@page "/components/aurora-background"

<PageTitle>AuroraBackground — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">AuroraBackground</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A decorative colour wash for the back of a section — blurred gradient blobs drifting behind
    the content. A layer, not a container: it takes no space, ignores the pointer, and is hidden
    from assistive tech.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The wrapper is <code>relative</code> and the layer is <code>absolute inset-0 -z-10</code>
    inside it, so it fills that wrapper and falls behind the copy. Supply the
    <code>relative</code> yourself — with no positioned ancestor the layer escapes to the
    viewport and covers the page.
</p>
<Example Source="AuroraBackgroundExample.razor"><AuroraBackgroundExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Still, and with the third blob</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>Animated="false"</code> freezes the field for a page that already moves for a reason;
    <code>Third</code> deepens it at the cost of more paint area.
</p>
<Example Source="AuroraBackgroundSection.razor"><AuroraBackgroundSection /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    It is the one element on the page that a screen reader will not read and that a printer will
    not show, so it can never be what makes something noticed. A new result, a saved state or an
    error has to be text and has to be in the DOM. The drift also stops on its own under
    <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>; if the movement is what you wanted, that is a design
    problem, not a setting to override.
</p>
